**Session 169 accomplished three things:**

1. **The RULE-5 consult on D-EX-GRANT-EPOCH-NOT-UNIQUE-TENURE-ID (#15) is done and the design is ruled.** GPT concurred with edge-triggered minting: `ex_grant_epoch` becomes a true tenure id — minted exactly when a node's continuous write-capable holding interval *starts* (judged from the grantee's holder bits in the pre-CAS compare image, never from `last_ex_slot`), preserved across PW↔EX mode changes, with a fail-closed probe when continuity is broken. The ruling also delivered a hardening list (explicit epoch copy on the preserve arm, conservative multi-mode classification, wrap-policy documentation duty) and — importantly for defect #1 — a new **enforcing-gate blocker**: a current-token-only manifest cannot prove an older-token record stale (release→reacquire leaves legitimate earlier-tenure records replay-required), so the equality gate needs a historical-record-lifetime invariant before it can ever refuse. Banked in `sess169-GPT-ruling-edge-mint-tenure-token`.

2. **The fix is half-landed: `caw_grant_epoch_update` is fully rewritten** (new 4-arg signature, mint/preserve/CONT-ZERO arms, P274 probes, wrap-injection hook), but the relay boundary hit mid-edit — **the tree does not currently build**. The three remaining mechanical edits (inject-knob declaration, `cur_slot` at the 5 call sites, removal of the dead `_orig` function) are itemized precisely in `sess169-edge-mint-HALF-LANDED-tree-does-not-build`, flagged as the next session's mandatory first job before any build/deploy/board.

3. **The memory compaction finally succeeded** after two failed attempts: `compiled-samenode-waiter-cancel-campaign` is written, folding and retiring all 21 sess111-125 campaign notes (root cause → STOP-SHIP rulings → clear-window linearization → owed worker) from every future listing.

Also verified en route: the two suspect mint sites at old lines 12977/13005 live in provably dead code (`_orig` has zero callers; the live single→multi flush deliberately promotes nothing), so the only live re-mint hazard was the upgrade arms the ruling now covers. Rig untouched: all 32 nodes remain board-ready on 0.11.460.

